1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:02,880
(Sheldon:)The two of them
now share a coffee can

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:04,380
(Sheldon:)on my mother's mantel.

3
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,880
(Howard:)So I knocked down
the bathroom door,

4
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:13,370
(Howard:)picked up my poor
unconscious mother,

5
00:00:13,370 --> 00:00:14,510
(Howard:)carried her to the car,

6
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:17,510
(Howard:)and drove like a madman
to the emergency room.

7
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:19,110
(Bernadette:)You're a real
hero, Howard.

8
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:21,380
(Howard:)No, I did what
any son would do.

9
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:25,020
(Penny:)Hang on a second--
you picked up your mother?

10
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:29,790
(Penny:)Her own legs
are barely able to do that.

11
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:33,020
(Howard:)I was filled
with adrenaline.

12
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,790
(Howard:)It happens to be how women
lift cars off babies.

13
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:38,730
(Penny:)Yeah, I'm saying,
it'd be easier to lift a car.

14
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:42,930
(Howard:)What can I tell you?
After I found the courage

15
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:45,670
(Howard:)to put her pants back on,
I was unstoppable.

16
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,640
(Leonard:)So, how is she?

17
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:50,600
(Howard:)They're running tests--
I don't know.

18
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,310
(Howard:)It may have been a heart attack
or heart-attack-like event.

19
00:00:54,310 --> 00:00:55,370
(Penny:)What's the difference?

20
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:57,110
(Sheldon:)A heart-attack-like event

21
00:00:57,110 --> 00:01:00,040
(Sheldon:)is an event
that's like a heart attack.

